---
import Lecture from '../../../layouts/Lecture.astro';
import CodePlayground from '../../../components/CodePlayground.astro';
import Callout from '../../../components/Callout.astro';
---

<Lecture
  chapterSlug="11-debugging"
  lessonSlug="02-read-traceback"
  hook="Parse a Python traceback as a string. Read it bottom-up: last line = error type, deepest frame = where the bug is."
>
  <h2>Anatomy</h2>
  <pre class="text-sm font-mono leading-6"><code>Traceback (most recent call last):
  File "letter_grade.py", line 19, in &lt;module&gt;
    print(letter_grade(85))
  File "letter_grade.py", line 12, in letter_grade   ← deepest frame, usually the bug
    return grade
NameError: name 'grade' is not defined              ← error type + message</code></pre>

  <h2>The two helpers</h2>
  <CodePlayground
    autoRun
    code={`def error_type(tb):
    last_line = tb.strip().splitlines()[-1]
    return last_line.split(":")[0].strip()

def last_frame(tb):
    filename = ""
    line_number = 0
    for raw in tb.splitlines():
        line = raw.strip()
        if line.startswith('File "'):
            rest = line[len('File "'):]
            close_q = rest.find('"')
            name = rest[:close_q]
            after = rest[close_q + 1:]
            i = after.find("line ")
            digits = ""
            for ch in after[i + 5:]:
                if ch.isdigit():
                    digits += ch
                else:
                    break
            filename = name
            line_number = int(digits)
    return (filename, line_number)

tb = '''Traceback (most recent call last):
  File "letter_grade.py", line 19, in <module>
    print(letter_grade(85))
  File "letter_grade.py", line 12, in letter_grade
    return grade
NameError: name 'grade' is not defined'''

print(error_type(tb))       # NameError
print(last_frame(tb))       # ('letter_grade.py', 12)`}
  />

  <Callout tone="tip" title="Why the deepest frame">
    <p>
      The bottom-most <code>File "..."</code> is where execution actually
      went wrong. The outer frames are just the call chain that got us
      there. <strong>Start at the bottom, work outward only if needed.</strong>
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>The common runtime errors</h2>
  <table class="text-sm">
    <thead><tr><th>Error</th><th>Most likely cause</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>NameError</code></td><td>Typo or used-before-defined</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>TypeError</code></td><td>Wrong type or arg count</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>IndexError</code></td><td>Index out of range</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>KeyError</code></td><td>Dict key not present</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>AttributeError ... NoneType ...</code></td><td>Function returned None; you called .x on it</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>RecursionError</code></td><td>Forgot the base case</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>ZeroDivisionError</code></td><td>Divided by 0</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</Lecture>
